# Bot & MCP Plugin Development Rules

## 1. Execution Workflow

- **Scan -> Implement -> Validate -> Push:** Never skip validation before updating a PR.
- Keep commits atomic and scoped to one enhancement wave at a time.

## 2. Speed & Reliability Standards

- **Async First:** Use non-blocking I/O and `Promise.all` (or equivalent concurrency/async batching) when querying multiple Dropbox endpoints or files.
- **Error Handling:** Wrap all external Dropbox API / MCP tool calls in try/catch blocks with actionable error messages (include status code and file path/ID).
- **Zero Breaking Changes:** Preserve existing tool names and parameter signatures unless explicitly told to deprecate them.

## 3. Code & Docs Hygiene

- Every new skill or MCP tool must have a matching update in the README/docs explaining its inputs, outputs, and usage example.
- Run typecheck/lint before every commit.
- For this repository, run `python3 mcp_host_skills_tests.py` and `python3 package_validation_tests.py` before every commit that touches plugins or skills.
